On 2/6/07, Cortesi <dcortesi@mindspring.com> wrote:

> la magrit. xusra du'u ti na tanko tubnu .i
> la magrit. natfe du'u ti tanko tubnu .i

Those need {lo} in front of {du'u}.

Also, {natfe} doesn't mean "deny" in the sense of "person x1 denies
that x2 is true". "Deny" is a pretty bad keyword, but what {natfe} means
is "proposition x1 contradicts proposition x2".

Perhaps {tolxusra} for "person x1 denies that x2 is true".

